Package: mouthtype-linux-desktop
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CodesWhat <80784472+scttbnsn@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: mouthtype-linux (= @VERSION@), python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-atspi-2.0, python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtqml, python3-pyside6.qtquick, python3-pyside6.qtnetwork, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-window, qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, qml6-module-qtqml-workerscript, qt6-svg-plugins, xdg-desktop-portal (>= 1.19)
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-kde, qml6-module-org-kde-layershell, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://mouthtype.app/linux/
Description: Mouthtype settings window and tray icon for GNOME and KDE Plasma
 The Qt settings window, tray icon and (on KDE Plasma) the floating recording
 pill for Mouthtype, built on PySide6. It talks to the mouthtype-linux daemon
 and reuses the same pages as the Omarchy bar plugin.
 .
 Install this on GNOME or KDE Plasma Wayland sessions. Omarchy and Hyprland
 installs only need mouthtype-linux and do not need this package or PySide6.
